  set:  # c211
    title: "smart-test per-PR gate blind to unmapped top-level paths (vendor hook dirs, .githooks, _shared subdirs) and to code covered only by the 19 map-unreachable root tests"  # c211
    fields:  # c211
      statement: "Every change that can break a test is exercised by the per-PR gate. STILL VIOLATED, RE-SCOPED (2026-08-01, dev 17cdf7393f): after WI-jozan (ca2fa7320e), WI-bisar (33b214f5ea), and WI-kahoj (1cc89c7170), smart-test selects tests for mapped top-level sources (single-component scripts/<name> and .agent/hooks/_shared/<name>.py|.sh, via separator-insensitive prefix match) and always runs edited root tests — but the gate remains structurally blind to (1) changes confined to paths the map does not claim: .agent/hooks/<vendor>/** (claude-code, codex-cli, cursor, gemini-cli), .githooks/**, subdirectories of _shared/, and (deliberately) scripts/lib/**; and (2) changes to code covered only by the 19 of 76 root tests (recounted 2026-08-01) that no name-based rule reaches (KNOWN_UNREACHABLE, tests/test_top_level_test_map.py:361-399 — including test_watcher_lifecycle.py, this item's original demonstration). In both cases smart-test writes a 0-test manifest and prints 'No Python source files changed - skipping tests' even though source files did change (scripts/smart-test:696-719, source-regex at :677 covers packages/*/src only), ci.yml:826-831 skips pytest, and regressions wait up to ~12h for the full-suite run. Adjacent defect: scripts/smart-test:678 defines CHANGED_TOP_LEVEL_SOURCES, which nothing reads, beneath a comment (:673-676) describing a skip-path check that does not exist."  # c211
- op: discuss  # 5f08
  at: '2026-08-01T04:58:55Z'  # 5f08
  by: agent  # 5f08
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5f08
  clock: 3  # 5f08
  nonce: 5f08  # 5f08
  message: "Premise re-verified on dev 17cdf7393f (2026-08-01). This invariant is roughly half drained: three merged commits fixed the mechanisms the original statement leaned on, but the per-PR gate remains structurally blind to a now-precisely-enumerable residual set. Everything below was re-derived from code and a fresh recount, not quoted from prior filings.\n\nFIXED SINCE FILING (three commits):\n1. ca2fa7320e (WI-jozan) added the top-level fold: scripts/smart-test lines 649-656 pipe changed files through .agent/hooks/_shared/top_level_test_map.py and union the result into AFFECTED_TESTS before the skip decision at line 680, so a mapped scripts/* or _shared/* change no longer skips pytest. The scripts/ hyphen-to-underscore collapse (auto-pr to auto_pr, map line 110) shipped HERE, not in WI-bisar — this item's root_cause field ('no hyphen normalisation') was already stale for scripts/ when filed; it was accurate only for _shared/ names.\n2. 33b214f5ea (WI-bisar, PR #105, closed done 2026-07-31) replaced the 1:1 exact match with a separator-insensitive prefix match (map lines 68-74 and 114-139; scripts/auto-pr now reaches 11 tests, pinned by tests/test_top_level_test_map.py lines 444-453), made _shared/ accept .sh as well as .py (lines 96-99; before, the guard was path.endswith('.py')), and added a two-sided real-tree ratchet (test file lines 426-441).\n3. 1cc89c7170 (WI-kahoj) made an edited test file always run, root tests/ included, unioned unconditionally (smart-test lines 658-671). That closes the 'or tests/' clause of the original statement: a changed root test can no longer be silently dropped. No later commit touches either file.\n\nSTILL LIVE (recounted 2026-08-01):\nA. The skip gate itself. smart-test line 677 defines source-changed as packages/*/src/*.py only; when the map returns nothing and no test was edited, lines 696-719 write a 0-test manifest whose reason line says 'no Python source files changed' and print 'No Python source files changed - skipping tests', then exit 0 — even when source files DID change. ci.yml lines 826-831 then skip pytest. Severity per WI-bisar's own correction: a feedback-latency gap of up to ~12 hours (full-suite's test-agent-infra job runs tests/ twice daily), not a permanent coverage hole.\nB. Vendor hook dirs are unmapped. top_level_test_map.py lines 92-111 accept only .agent/hooks/_shared/ and single-component scripts/ paths. Measured today: map_to_tests returns an empty list for .agent/hooks/claude-code/session-start.sh, .agent/hooks/gemini-cli/before-model-transcript.sh, .githooks/reference-transaction, and scripts/lib/pool_utils.py (the last is the documented deliberate exclusion). A change confined to .agent/hooks/claude-code|codex-cli|cursor|gemini-cli/** runs zero tests per-PR.\nC. Recount: 76 root tests now exist (was 73 at WI-bisar close); 57 are reachable from some top-level source via the map (fed all 95 candidates: every file in scripts/ plus every .py/.sh in _shared/); 19 are unreachable (was 18 — three tests added since: test_smart_test.py and test_check_mypy_ratchet_blocking.py reachable, test_forge_github_harness.py exempt). The 19 exactly equal KNOWN_UNREACHABLE in tests/test_top_level_test_map.py lines 361-399, so the ratchet holds — but ratchet-exempt still means per-PR dark: a change to code covered only by those 19 selects nothing and hits path A. Notably test_watcher_lifecycle.py, the exact red test in this invariant's original 2026-07-29 demonstration, is among the 19; that demonstration would reproduce today.\nD. smart-test line 678 defines CHANGED_TOP_LEVEL_SOURCES and nothing ever reads it (single occurrence in the file). The comment above it (lines 673-676) says top-level sources 'are included via a separate check so the no-source-files skip path respects them' — no check consults this variable; the real mechanism is the fold at lines 649-656. The dead regex also accepts only .py under _shared while the live map accepts .sh, so wiring it up unchanged would reintroduce the .sh blindness WI-bisar removed.\n\nWHAT THIS ITEM NOW MEANS: not 'smart-test skips all scripts/ and hook changes' (fixed for the mapped set), but: the per-PR gate is blind to (1) top-level paths outside the map's claimed domain — vendor hook dirs, .githooks/**, _shared subdirectories, scripts/lib/** — and (2) code covered only by the 19 behaviour-named/multi-source root tests no name-based rule can reach; and in both cases it reports the blindness with a false 'No Python source files changed' message. Statement re-scoped accordingly; status stays violated. Not re-running the original repro end-to-end was a constraint of this verification pass (smart-test is lock-guarded and mutates .ci/affected-tests.txt); the evidence here is code-path plus direct invocation of the map's own map_to_tests function."  # 5f08
- op: discuss  # 1702
  at: '2026-08-01T05:31:07Z'  # 1702
  by: agent  # 1702
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1702
  clock: 4  # 1702
  nonce: '1702'  # 1702
  message: "SUBSTANTIALLY DRAINED by PR #142 (dev 54a5f34bcc, 2026-08-01) — the\ntrust-substrate fix. What landed, mapped to this item's re-scoped limbs:\n\n  (1) Unmapped top-level paths — CLOSED with over-selection. Any changed\n      file under scripts/ (any depth), .githooks/, or .agent/hooks/ that\n      top_level_test_map.py cannot reach now unions the ENTIRE root suite\n      into the selection, disclosed in the log. Vendor hook dirs are now\n      ALSO name-mapped with an existence-checked parity floor\n      (test_touch_heartbeat + test_session_start_respawn), so vendor\n      changes select their wiring tests precisely rather than only via\n      fallback. .githooks/** stays deliberately unmapped (decision recorded\n      in the map docstring); the fallback covers it broadly.\n  (2) The dead CHANGED_TOP_LEVEL_SOURCES variable and its false comment are\n      gone; the variable is now the live trigger for the fallback.\n  (3) The false skip message is gone: the 0-test manifest branch is\n      reachable only for genuinely docs/config-only changes and its wording\n      says so.\n\nLIVE REPRO (the item's own demonstration shape, re-run 2026-08-01): an\nUNTRACKED, unmapped file (touch scripts/zz-probe-unmapped-inv-lizor.sh)\nfollowed by smart-test --manifest produced Mode: targeted, Selected\ntests: 77 (the full root suite). Pre-fix, the same probe produced a 0-test\nmanifest and the false message. The probe also exercises the untracked\nroute: enumeration now includes git ls-files --others --exclude-standard,\nscoped so pending tracker .ops files cannot leak in.\n\nSTILL OPEN, honestly scoped — status stays violated:\n  (a) A source that name-maps to SOME test does not trigger the fallback,\n      so coverage living additionally in a map-unreachable test (the 19\n      KNOWN_UNREACHABLE, now vendor-aware) can still be skipped for that\n      source. Drain path: the declarative covers: marker the map docstring\n      names; the ratchet keeps the 19 from growing.\n  (b) INV-kinin route 7 (CLI-driven sole-coverer tests invisible to the\n      import slice on IN-scope changes) is out of this fix's reach by\n      construction — it needs coverage-map selection, recorded there.\nAlso: the two-sided KNOWN_UNREACHABLE ratchet caught the fix's own author —\nthe day-old test_transcript_permissions.py was name-unreachable ('perms'\nis not a prefix of 'permissions'), renamed test_transcript_perms.py in the\nsame PR. The gate the item complains about now polices its own additions."  # 1702
